Short interpretation
The interactive figures provide the values used in the report comparisons. They do not replace the Korean report.
Most comparisons require three safeguards:

separate total citation counts from citations per DOI-citing policy document;
separate citations to Korean research from citations made by Korean policy documents;
check whether the denominator changes before comparing percentages.

Verification without licensed source data
The public verification script recomputes:

the combined U.S., IGO, and U.K. policy-source share for citations to Korean research;
the U.S. research share cited by Korean policy documents;
the social- and health-science shares in the two Korea-related directions;
the 36.1% U.S. domain-adjusted reference value;
baseline counts used in the author-country sensitivity analysis; and
whether the country-domain cache matches the sequential country-assignment rule and the recorded parquet size and modification time.

Extract both archives into the same directory and run:
python scripts/verify_public_report_aggregates.py --root . --run-tag 20251026
A successful run ends with PUBLIC_AGGREGATE_VERIFICATION=PASS. This audit verifies the report’s public aggregate layer; it does not recreate licensed Overton source records.
